  "notes": "ALU's official 2025 University Catalog (Version 2) publishes course groupings (core, general education, electives) with total credits, semester count and credits per semester, but does not publish a term-by-term course sequence. Semesters below distribute the catalog's required courses evenly across the catalog-stated 5 semesters x 12 credits, with foundational general education first and catalog-stated prerequisites observed (prereq course placed in an earlier semester). Actual term placement is set with an ALU advisor via the Individual Degree Plan.\nALU awards 'units'; the catalog's tuition schedule prices tuition per SEMESTER CREDIT HOUR, so units are treated as semester credits here.\nCore (24 cr): ACC201, BUS110, BUS220, BUS240, BUS254, BUS325, BUS350, MGT214. General education (21 cr): ACC200, BUS330, CMP101, COM100, ENG160, ENG170, MAT140. Electives (15 cr): five courses from ACC, BUS, FIN, LGS, CJS. Prerequisites per catalog course descriptions: ACC201 requires ACC200; ENG170 requires ENG160; BUS254 and BUS325 require BUS110; BUS330 requires MGT214.",
